repository-code: "https://github.com/gkerherve/KherveBook"
keywords:
  - computational notebook
  - scientific computing
  - Python
  - reproducible research
  - spreadsheet
  - LaTeX
abstract: >-
  KherveBook is an open-source, Jupyter-inspired computational notebook
  implemented as a native Qt desktop application with its own in-process
  Python kernel. A single document mixes six cell types: runnable Python,
  Markdown, LaTeX (typeset via tectonic), live spreadsheets two-way linked
  to Python, SVG drawings, and JavaScript/HTML. It ships ~180 built-in
  scientific examples, an AI assistant, per-notebook Git version history,
  and lossless Jupyter .ipynb import/export.
